==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|in the hell}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ðəˈhɛl/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-the hell.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|sometimes|vulgar}} {{non-gloss|Used to indicate [[emphatic]] [[rejection]] of an assertion or request.}}
#: {{syn|en|like hell|the hell you say|hell|q3=postpositional}}
#: {{ux|en|A: I can run faster than a horse.<br>B: '''The hell''' you can!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1990|author=Stephen King|title={{w|The Moving Finger (short story)|The Moving Finger}}
|passage='You stay here, sir,' O'Bannion instructed.<br>''''The hell''' I will,' Feeney said.}}
# {{lb|en|sometimes|vulgar}} {{non-gloss|[[expletive|Expletive]] used for [[emphasis]], typically after an [[interrogative]] term or [[relative pronoun]].}}
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:the dickens}}
#: {{ux|en|What '''the hell''' was that?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Body Politic|year=1971|number=1|page=3|title=Oxside In A Closet|author=Allan Oxside|text=I thought we were all sisters and brothers I guess I am not accepted. I sure wish '''the hell''' I stayed in the closet.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=17 Dec 89|volume=17|number=23|journal=Gay Community News|page=11|author=Christopher Wittke|title=On The Edge In The '80s|text=D'Allesandro was particularly adept at that kind of flash-forward-then-backward-all-'''the-hell'''-over-the-place kind of narrative and like a tourist following a well-seasoned guide, you never lose track of the line.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2009 February 19|author=Gareth Lewis|url=http://www.dailyecho.co.uk/leisure/hampshire_food_festival_2015/4139634.Hampshire_pub__has_gone_down_the_khazi__says_top_critic/|work=Southern Daily Echo|passage=“Whoever '''the hell''' is running the place now has made a terrible mess of it,” he said... “Not in the sense that it looks different, or that it isn't pretty much permanently full. It's just that the food as [[go down the khazi|gone utterly down the khazi]].”|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260623104314/https://www.dailyecho.co.uk/leisure/hampshire_food_festival_2015/4139634.Hampshire_pub__has_gone_down_the_khazi__says_top_critic/|archivedate=23 June 2026}}

